<point name="prime_spawn" color="0.15 0.9 0.35" box="-8 -8 0 8 8 28">
  Prime player spawn. Supports neutral and every native team, exact facing, nullable label and stable identity. Origin is the native feet position.
  <string key="prime_id" name="Persistent Prime GUID">New and cloned objects receive a new GUID when saved by Project Prime Radiant. Preserve this identity for existing objects.</string>
  <real3 key="origin" name="Position (Quake units)">Prime x,y,z maps to Quake x,-z,y using project source scale. No player-height offset.</real3>
  <string key="prime_label" name="Label" value="">Plain text unless the encoding field selects Base64 UTF-8. Backslashes are literal.</string>
  <prime_boolean key="prime_label_is_null" name="Label is null" value="false">True preserves a null native label; false allows an empty string. Null labels require an empty label value.</prime_boolean>
  <prime_label_encoding_type key="prime_label_encoding" name="Label encoding" value="plain">Exceptional labels containing quotes or control characters use Base64 UTF-8 to survive native Quake serialization.</prime_label_encoding_type>
  <prime_team_type key="prime_team" name="Team" value="-1"></prime_team_type>
  <angle key="angle" name="Facing (Quake degrees)" value="-90">Standard native rotation gizmo heading. Prime heading equals Quake heading plus 90 degrees.</angle>
  <real key="prime_yaw" name="Facing (Prime degrees)" value="0">Exact authored Prime yaw. Editing this field is supported; do not make conflicting edits to both headings.</real>
  <real key="prime_angle_baseline" name="Facing baseline (preserve)" value="-90">Exported Quake heading baseline distinguishes gizmo rotation from direct Prime yaw edits. Preserve this metadata.</real>
</point>
<point name="prime_pickup" color="1 0.75 0.15" box="-7 -7 0 7 7 16">
  Prime multiplayer pickup. Every supported native pickup type is available, with base policy and respawn interval.
  <string key="prime_id" name="Persistent Prime GUID">New and cloned objects receive a new GUID when saved by Project Prime Radiant. Preserve this identity for existing objects.</string>
  <real3 key="origin" name="Position (Quake units)">Prime x,y,z maps to Quake x,-z,y using project source scale. No player-height offset.</real3>
  <string key="prime_label" name="Label" value="">Plain text unless the encoding field selects Base64 UTF-8. Backslashes are literal.</string>
  <prime_boolean key="prime_label_is_null" name="Label is null" value="false">True preserves a null native label; false allows an empty string. Null labels require an empty label value.</prime_boolean>
  <prime_label_encoding_type key="prime_label_encoding" name="Label encoding" value="plain">Exceptional labels containing quotes or control characters use Base64 UTF-8 to survive native Quake serialization.</prime_label_encoding_type>
  <prime_pickup_type key="prime_type" name="Pickup type" value="MissileSmall"></prime_pickup_type>
  <prime_boolean key="prime_has_base" name="Show base" value="true"></prime_boolean>
  <integer key="prime_spawn_interval" name="Respawn simulation frames" value="300">Unsigned 16-bit interval, 0 through 65535.</integer>
</point>
<point name="prime_jumppad" color="0.3 0.7 1" box="-12 -12 0 12 12 8">
  Prime jump pad. Choose exactly one non-null target or direction. Target positions use scaled Quake coordinates; directions use Quake axes without source scale. Size uses positive Quake x/y/z dimensions.
  <string key="prime_id" name="Persistent Prime GUID">New and cloned objects receive a new GUID when saved by Project Prime Radiant. Preserve this identity for existing objects.</string>
  <real3 key="origin" name="Position (Quake units)">Prime x,y,z maps to Quake x,-z,y using project source scale. No player-height offset.</real3>
  <string key="prime_label" name="Label" value="">Plain text unless the encoding field selects Base64 UTF-8. Backslashes are literal.</string>
  <prime_boolean key="prime_label_is_null" name="Label is null" value="false">True preserves a null native label; false allows an empty string. Null labels require an empty label value.</prime_boolean>
  <prime_label_encoding_type key="prime_label_encoding" name="Label encoding" value="plain">Exceptional labels containing quotes or control characters use Base64 UTF-8 to survive native Quake serialization.</prime_label_encoding_type>
  <prime_boolean key="prime_target_is_null" name="Target is null" value="false"></prime_boolean>
  <real3 key="prime_target" name="Target (absolute Quake units)" value="0 0 64"></real3>
  <prime_boolean key="prime_vector_is_null" name="Direction is null" value="true"></prime_boolean>
  <real3 key="prime_vector" name="Direction (unscaled Quake axes)" value="0 0 1"></real3>
  <real key="prime_speed" name="Native launch speed" value="1">Positive in direction mode; target mode preserves this authored field.</real>
  <real3 key="prime_size" name="Trigger dimensions (Quake units)" value="25.6 25.6 28.8"></real3>
  <integer key="prime_model_id" name="Native model ID" value="0">Unsigned 32-bit native model identifier.</integer>
  <integer key="prime_cooldown_time" name="Cooldown frames" value="20">Unsigned 16-bit frame count.</integer>
  <integer key="prime_control_lock_time" name="Control lock frames" value="30">Unsigned 16-bit frame count.</integer>
</point>
<point name="prime_navigation_link" color="1 0.35 0.85" box="-5 -5 -5 5 5 5">
  Prime navigation link. Origin is From. To is an absolute Quake position. Native node hints and traversal kind are preserved. Moving the link moves its authored endpoints together.
  <string key="prime_id" name="Persistent Prime GUID">New and cloned objects receive a new GUID when saved by Project Prime Radiant. Preserve this identity for existing objects.</string>
  <real3 key="origin" name="Position (Quake units)">Prime x,y,z maps to Quake x,-z,y using project source scale. No player-height offset.</real3>
  <real3 key="prime_to" name="To (absolute Quake units)" value="32 0 0"></real3>
  <prime_link_kind key="prime_kind" name="Traversal kind" value="Manual"></prime_link_kind>
  <prime_boolean key="prime_bidirectional" name="Bidirectional" value="false"></prime_boolean>
  <prime_node_kind key="prime_from_node_kind" name="From node kind" value="Auto"></prime_node_kind>
  <prime_node_kind key="prime_to_node_kind" name="To node kind" value="Auto"></prime_node_kind>
</point>
<point name="prime_trigger" color="0.7 0.3 1" box="-6 -6 -6 6 6 6">
  Prime Q3 traversal trigger. Origin is the native minimum corner transformed to Quake axes; bounds maximum is the transformed native maximum corner. Quake Y decreases toward native maximum Z. Volume and destination are edited numerically here; brush-shaped volume handles remain a parity task.
  <string key="prime_id" name="Persistent Prime GUID">New and cloned objects receive a new GUID when saved by Project Prime Radiant. Preserve this identity for existing objects.</string>
  <real3 key="origin" name="Position (Quake units)">Prime x,y,z maps to Quake x,-z,y using project source scale. No player-height offset.</real3>
  <real3 key="prime_bounds_max" name="Bounds maximum corner (Quake units)" value="32 -32 32">Absolute transformed Prime maximum corner, not sorted Quake bounds. Moving the volume translates both authored corners.</real3>
  <real3 key="prime_destination" name="Destination/apex (absolute Quake units)" value="0 0 64"></real3>
  <prime_trigger_kind key="prime_kind" name="Trigger kind" value="push"></prime_trigger_kind>
  <integer key="prime_source_entity" name="Original BSP entity (provenance)" value="0">0 through 32767. Source provenance only; duplicate source numbers are valid. Persistent identity is prime_id.</integer>
  <angle key="angle" name="Facing (Quake degrees)" value="-90">Standard native rotation gizmo heading. Prime heading equals Quake heading plus 90 degrees.</angle>
  <real key="prime_yaw" name="Facing (Prime degrees)" value="0">Exact authored Prime yaw. Editing this field is supported; do not make conflicting edits to both headings.</real>
  <real key="prime_angle_baseline" name="Facing baseline (preserve)" value="-90">Exported Quake heading baseline distinguishes gizmo rotation from direct Prime yaw edits. Preserve this metadata.</real>
  <real key="prime_gravity" name="Gravity (Prime units per second squared)" value="50">Greater than zero, at most 10000.</real>
  <integer key="prime_cooldown_frames" name="Cooldown simulation frames" value="30">1 through 600.</integer>
</point>
</classes>
